# React coding style

`frontend/` is Next.js 16 (App Router) and React 19. Match the surrounding file instead of restyling a directory.

## Files and names

- `.tsx` for JSX. `.ts` for logic and types that do not render.
- Pages live in `frontend/app/`. Feature components live in `frontend/components/<area>/`. Shared UI lives in `frontend/components/ui/`.
- Tests live under `frontend/__tests__/` so Vitest runs them (`**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}`).
- Event handlers inside a component are `handleClick` / `handleSubmit`. The prop that receives one is `onClick` / `onSubmit`.
- The app uses Tailwind. Do not add a CSS-module layout for one screen.

## Components

Prefer a closed `type Props` and destructure props in the parameter list. Use `interface` when the type is an extension point that already uses one.

Self-close tags with no children. Use a fragment when no DOM node is needed. Keep multi-line conditions above the `return` instead of inside JSX.

New class components are not allowed. When a change is already non-trivial, convert a class component you are editing to a function.

## Server and client

- `"use client"` goes on line 1, before imports, and only when the file uses state, effects, refs, browser APIs, or event handlers.
- Keep the directive on a file that already has it unless you are sure the file no longer needs the client runtime.
- Do not import server-only modules (secrets, database clients) from a client module.
- Do not re-export server-only code through a client file.

## Imports and state

React imports first, then third-party packages, then project imports. Use `import type` for type-only bindings.

Local state stays in the component that uses it. Lift it when a parent and child share it. Server data goes through TanStack Query (`QueryProvider`). Auth, notifications, and settings already have context. Do not add another global store.

Call `useState` and other `use*` functions unconditionally at the top of the component. The state-and-effects rule has the rest.
